against all advice i did work full-time  during my first three years of studying  medicine at university and although i'm  not going to get into whether that was  the best decision in the world in this  video today as you can imagine it did  mean that when it came to completing  university projects i didn't always have  the luxury of time so whether i liked it  or not i did have to come up with  systems to do things fastly efficiently  and without procrastinating  now although i definitely do not condone  leaving things to the last minute i do  agree that systems do make things that  are not so enjoyable be a lot more  efficient and therefore fun today i  wanted to share the exact system that i  used to write good university essays in  under three hours by doing a full  walkthrough of an essay with you here so  i have my computer in front of me and  let's get started so first things first  i am going to be using notion this is  because it is literally the best app in  the world i have a whole second brain on  it if you want to check that out there's  a video somewhere if you're into that  but basically notion is free it's clean  it's effective it's absolutely in my  opinion the best app for students now  you can probably use the system with  something else but i'm going to be doing  my walkthrough in notion i'll break down  every single step in a way that should  hopefully be easy to replicate so let's  say our essay title is the importance of  teaching skills in medical professional  practice this is an essay i had to write  last year the first thing i'm going to  do is create a database page on notion  now this sounds really complicated all  it really is is a table so it's quite  easy to work with now the reason i do  this is because i absolutely hate  writing essays top to bottom i actually  write them left to right and i'm going  to explain how this happens i think it's  a hugely heavy lift to write a full  essay so i kind of break it up into very  many small bits the first breakup that i  will do is obviously an introduction  body and conclusion because we have to  start write and wrap up our essay now  there's an extra step that i do here  that i feel is very important i feel an  easy way that people lose points with  their essays is not looking at the  marking scheme and no matter how  elaborate beautiful how many amazing  points you make and how many great  quotes that you use in your essay if you  are not taking all of the criteria in  the marking points you are obviously  going to lose a lot of marks and on the  flip side if you take every single point  in the marking scheme even if you  haven't written an amazing essay you are  guaranteed a pass or even a really good  mark so i go to the marketing scheme and  make sure i do all of them sometimes i  have essays which don't have such a  delicate marking scheme and in this case  i will have to come up with it myself  okay what do i think this professor  would like to assess me on and i put  those points in the body this should  take about five to ten minutes depending  on if you are copy pasting these from  somewhere else or if i'm just spending a  few minutes kind of trying to come up  with them myself i don't spend a lot of  time on this part step number two is  when we start to branch out a bit so  i'll be thinking about the introduction  itself this is where i set the scene for  the essay the way that i imagine  introductions is like  i'm having a conversation with someone  who's in front of me who does not know  the title of my essay and i'm not  allowed to say the title of my essay but  i can talk about whatever so i just kind  of set the context in a way that i  try to make the person ask the question  which is the title of the essay itself  if that makes any sense and if you can  write from mind around that so in this  case i think i'm going to start by  writing why it's important for a doctor  to be a teacher and that's going to be  my first paragraph and my second  paragraph is going to talk about why i'm  writing this essay at all and kind of  the experiences that i did and i think  this would be fine for the introduction  now within the body i'm going to go to  every single assessment point and create  an aim for every single paragraph and  some of these assessment points won't  stand on paragraphs as their own so i'll  just kind of remove them some of them i  might want to merge together but for  every single one i'm going to see if  they can stand as a future paragraph so  for the conclusion i do the exact same  thing i think i want to end this essay  by talking about the wider context of  higher education and its implications  for professional medical practice then  i'm also going to talk about somehow how  this experience has changed me um this  column two is now done and this should  take about 20 minutes i think to kind of  make these points and clean these things  up it's only about 10 sentences that i'm  actually writing but it does take a bit  of thinking time step number three is  where we start to have fun for every  single aim i created i'm going to make a  central core argument for each paragraph  i think where essays don't look very  good is where paragraphs are quite  wishy-washy and when i read them i'm not  sure what they're saying or what point  they are trying to make so trying to  approach it from the other way around  where you make the central point of the  paragraph first and then you build the  paragraph ensures that everything that  you're writing has a central aim and is  very coherent and logical so for every  single aim and this can be either the  marking criteria or it can be the things  that i put in the introduction and  conclusion i am going to make one single  argument and these arguments don't all  have to come from my brain very often i  like using quotes here i like using  studies i like using kind of experiences  of my own so it can be very different  things i cheat on this point because i  have a second brain so i have all of  these quotes and studies in one place  already so i've had to double the time  that it takes me to do this in this  three hour estimation for example if i  want to talk about the importance of  being a doctor in medicine i like this  richard feynman quote which says a young  man doesn't realize how much time it  takes to prepare good lectures for the  first time especially it kind of talks  about how students or people who haven't  talked before don't appreciate how  difficult and important education is and  therefore i think this is a quote for  someone famous it is written well and it  also makes a good point so i'm going to  be using this quote as my central  argument for my first paragraph and i'll  do the same thing for every single other  paragraph i spend a lot of time on  pubmed here trying to find studies that  have findings or explorations which are  relevant to the points that i want to  make in my study and very importantly  here i'll also add another column with  the sources so for every single quote or  every single study i will have the full  source of it so i can use it in my kind  of resources in the end of my essay so  for me this takes maximum half an hour  but i can see how it can take up to an  hour so at this point we have done one  and a half hour of our essay writing  already and this is where we get to step  number four and this is the only time  where i actually start writing the words  of my essay and why i find the system  works so well is because if i were to  start from scratch i would have to write  kind of a whole essay based on nothing  but because i have all of these kind of  rows done what that means is that it's  kind of like i have someone who's just  prepared most of my essay for me already  and i don't have to write a full essay  all i have to write is paragraphs based  on a single argument which is very easy  to do so for example for the  introduction itself if i said i want to  talk about why education in medicine is  important using this quote from richard  baineman that actually becomes a very  easy paragraph to write it's only going  to be a few sentences of me kind of  elaborating on this aim that i've  already made and i've done the same  thing everywhere so for example i'm  talking about the importance of using  imagery in education based on the fact  that there's the study that found that  using images improves learning so much  all i need to do is just elaborate on  that and add some extra words adverbs  and sentences it's not actually very  hard to do this honestly for me makes  writing endlessly easier and this part  usually takes me about an hour maximum  to do and when i am finally done with  this i feel super super relieved all i  do is take all the paragraphs that i've  written which are the actual essay  content and i put them together but at  this point i'm kind of blind to the  essay i have the same thing when i'm  working for something for a long time so  when i finish a painting i can't  actually see it normally and when i  finish an essay i can't actually see the  essay because i'm too used to the words  so i kind of need to take a break and a  few hours of this will do but a few days  is absolutely perfect depending on how  last minute this task has been left to  be so um i'll kind of step away from my  essay and i'll only come back to it  later and give it another half an hour  where i read through it make sure  everything makes sense i might rearrange  things delete or add some sentences here  and there and make sure it is all  coherent all my sources are already  listed so i can just copy and paste  those too and yep that is three hours of  work and a full essay done which has all  of the marking criteria sorted it has  all the resources there already it's  kind of creative because it has a bunch  of extra quotes and kind of fun things  in it it is structured well every single  paragraph is making a point which is  tied to the aim of the essay itself so  yeah it's kind of hard to go wrong using  this method so beyond the essay itself  this is actually a very special video  for me because it is my first notion  sponsorship and i am endlessly grateful  for them i knew during this video that i  wanted to do something related to  education because  um even though i have my completely  over-the-top uses for notion actually  it's just the best thing for students to  use in general and i thought that if i  were to make it a notion video it would  have to be for students so yeah here it  is i hope this made sense to anyone else  i'll be going back to university next  year so i will definitely be needing any  tips for essay writing and for studying  so if you have anything to share please  feel free to do so in the comments if  you haven't already signed up for notion  i'd be very surprised but there will be  a link in my description which will give  you free access to the app but otherwise  thank you so much for spending this time  with me i hope you have a wonderful rest  of your day be kind to yourself and  others and don't believe everything you  think and loads loads of luck with your  essays in university bye

